{%- comment -%}
  Account link for new customer accounts.
  Logged out  → new customer accounts login (returns to wholesale dashboard)
  Wholesale   → wholesale dashboard on your store
  Everyone else → Shopify account (orders)
{%- endcomment -%}

{% comment %} {%- liquid
  assign account_label = 'Account'

  unless customer
    capture account_href
      render 'customer-login-url'
    endcapture
    assign account_href = account_href | strip
  endunless

  if customer
    if customer.tags contains 'wholesale'
      assign account_href = '/pages/wholesale-dashboard'
      if customer.first_name != blank
        assign account_label = customer.first_name
      endif
    else
      assign account_href = routes.account_url
      if customer.first_name != blank
        assign account_label = customer.first_name
      endif
    endif
  endif
-%}

<a
  class="header__icon-touch header__icon-touch--account"
  href="{{ account_href }}"
  aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.go_account' | t }}"
>
  {% render 'icon-button' with icon: 'header-account' %}
  <span class="text-account">{{ account_label }}</span>
</a> {% endcomment %}
{%- comment -%}
  Header account link/icon.

  Behavior:
  - Logged in: unchanged — plain link to the account page (or wholesale dashboard).
  - Logged out: hovering the account link (desktop) reveals a small preview
    popup. Clicking the link (any device) opens a full sign-in panel that
    slides in from the right. Clicking the link still points to the real
    login URL, so it degrades gracefully if JS is unavailable.

  All copy below is customizable by passing params when rendering this
  snippet, e.g.:

    {% render 'header-account', popup_heading: section.settings.popup_heading %}

  Every variable falls back to the exact copy from the reference design if
  nothing is passed in. See the bottom of this file for the full list of
  variable names, and the accompanying message for a schema settings array
  you can paste into the section that renders this snippet.
{%- endcomment -%}

